    "body": "Your friend, sitting on a stool at rest, is handed a bicycle wheel (figure on left) of mass \\textbf{m = 2 kg} and radius \\textbf{R = 0.58 m}, spinning with an angular velocity $\\mathbf{\\omega}$ = $\\mathbf{<0, 11, 0> rad/s}$. Your friend then abruptly flips the wheel (figure on right) such that is continues to rotate with the same angular speed, but in exactly the opposite direction.\n\nWhat is your friend's \\textbf{angular velocity} immediately after your friend flips the bicycle wheel? The bicycle wheel can be modeled as a hoop ($I_{hoop} = mR^2$). Your friend  can be modeled as a cylinder ($I_{cylinder} = \\frac{1}{2}Mr^2$) of mass \\textbf{M = 80 kg} and radius \\textbf{r = 0.40 m}.",
